{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789817810233,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_30f47f4cfef64954a1b2be75","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\opencode.log"},"output":"<path>C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\opencode.log</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: COMMAND: \"C:/Users/kelly/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe\" run --format json --auto --dir \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project\" --file \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\" --title \"SAI Reviewer Test\" \"You are generating an interactive comprehensive exam system for a web app.\n2: \n3: STEP 1: Load the skill named  interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator  using your skill tool. Follow ALL of its instructions exactly (chapter organization of ~30 questions/chapter, timed/untimed modes, overall exam, answer key, encyclopedia, anti-guessing rules, balanced answers, stable question IDs, explanation for every question).\n4: \n5: STEP 2: The reference material is a PDF attached to your message, located at:\n6: C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\n7: \n8: Read it with your Read tool. It is the PRIMARY SOURCE OF TRUTH. Do not invent facts unsupported by it. Identify its chapters/lessons and build a coverage plan, then generate the question bank.\n9: \n10: STEP 3: Write the question bank as ONE valid JSON object EXACTLY to this file:\n11: C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/questions.json\n12: \n13: Do NOT create any HTML, CSS, JS, markdown, or other files. Do NOT print the JSON in your final reply; just write the file.\n14: \n15: Use EXACTLY this JSON schema:\n16: \n17: {\n18:    title :  Full exam title ,\n19:    subject :  Subject or course name ,\n20:    summary :  One short paragraph about coverage ,\n21:    chapters : [\n22:     {\n23:        chapterId :  ch1 ,\n24:        title :  Name of chapter/lesson 1 ,\n25:        description :  Short description of this chapter ,\n26:        questions : [\n27:         {\n28:            id :  ch1-q01 ,\n29:            question :  The question text. Use scenarios, comparisons, exceptions, application and analysis, not just recall. ,\n30:            choices : [ Choice A text ,  Choice B text ,  Choice C text ,  Choice D text ],\n31:            correctAnswer : 0,\n32:            explanation :  Concise explanation of why this is correct and why the others are not. \n33:         }\n34:       ]\n35:     }\n36:   ],\n37:    encyclopedia : [\n38:     {  chapterId :  ch1 ,  term :  Important term ,  definition :  Definition grounded in the reference.  }\n39:   ]\n40: }\n41: \n42: HARD RULES for the JSON:\n43: - correctAnswer is the 0-based INDEX of the correct choice within the choices array.\n44: - Every question MUST have exactly 4 choices and exactly one correct answer.\n45: - Every question MUST have id, question, choices, correctAnswer, explanation.\n46: - Every chapter MUST have chapterId, title, description, and at least 1 question.\n47: - Approximately 30 questions per chapter (fewer if the chapter is thin, never fabricate).\n48: - Balanced A/B/C/D correct-answer positions overall; no obvious answer patterns.\n49: - All-choice parity: correct answer must not be the longest/most technical/most specific option.\n50: - Explanations must be grounded in the reference.\n51: - encyclopedia MUST contain the important terms from the reference, at least 10 entries unless the reference is very small.\n52: - The JSON MUST be valid. Check it before writing.\n53: \n54: After writing the file, reply with a one-line confirmation telling me the exact path of the JSON file you wrote.\" 2>&1\n55: \n\n(End of file - total 55 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"COMMAND: \"C:/Users/kelly/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe\" run --format json --auto --dir \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project\" --file \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\" --title \"SAI Reviewer Test\" \"You are generating an interactive comprehensive exam system for a web app.\n\nSTEP 1: Load the skill named  interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator  using your skill tool. Follow ALL of its instructions exactly (chapter organization of ~30 questions/chapter, timed/untimed modes, overall exam, answer key, encyclopedia, anti-guessing rules, balanced answers, stable question IDs, explanation for every question).\n\nSTEP 2: The reference material is a PDF attached to your message, located at:\nC:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\n\nRead it with your Read tool. It is the PRIMARY SOURCE OF TRUTH. Do not invent facts unsupported by it. Identify its chapters/lessons and build a coverage plan, then generate the question bank.\n\nSTEP 3: Write the question bank as ONE valid JSON object EXACTLY to this file:\nC:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/questions.json\n\nDo NOT create any HTML, CSS, JS, markdown, or other files. Do NOT print the JSON in your final reply; just write the file.\n\nUse EXACTLY this JSON schema:\n\n{\n   title :  Full exam title ,\n   subject :  Subject or course name ,\n   summary :  One short paragraph about coverage ,","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\opencode.log","text":"COMMAND: \"C:/Users/kelly/AppData/Roaming/npm/node_modules/opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe\" run --format json --auto --dir \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project\" --file \"C:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\" --title \"SAI Reviewer Test\" \"You are generating an interactive comprehensive exam system for a web app.\n\nSTEP 1: Load the skill named  interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator  using your skill tool. Follow ALL of its instructions exactly (chapter organization of ~30 questions/chapter, timed/untimed modes, overall exam, answer key, encyclopedia, anti-guessing rules, balanced answers, stable question IDs, explanation for every question).\n\nSTEP 2: The reference material is a PDF attached to your message, located at:\nC:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/source.pdf\n\nRead it with your Read tool. It is the PRIMARY SOURCE OF TRUTH. Do not invent facts unsupported by it. Identify its chapters/lessons and build a coverage plan, then generate the question bank.\n\nSTEP 3: Write the question bank as ONE valid JSON object EXACTLY to this file:\nC:/xampp/htdocs/automation/side-project/data/exams/test001/questions.json\n\nDo NOT create any HTML, CSS, JS, markdown, or other files. Do NOT print the JSON in your final reply; just write the file.\n\nUse EXACTLY this JSON schema:\n\n{\n   title :  Full exam title ,\n   subject :  Subject or course name ,\n   summary :  One short paragraph about coverage ,\n   chapters : [\n    {\n       chapterId :  ch1 ,\n       title :  Name of chapter/lesson 1 ,\n       description :  Short description of this chapter ,\n       questions : [\n        {\n           id :  ch1-q01 ,\n           question :  The question text. Use scenarios, comparisons, exceptions, application and analysis, not just recall. ,\n           choices : [ Choice A text ,  Choice B text ,  Choice C text ,  Choice D text ],\n           correctAnswer : 0,\n           explanation :  Concise explanation of why this is correct and why the others are not. \n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n   encyclopedia : [\n    {  chapterId :  ch1 ,  term :  Important term ,  definition :  Definition grounded in the reference.  }\n  ]\n}\n\nHARD RULES for the JSON:\n- correctAnswer is the 0-based INDEX of the correct choice within the choices array.\n- Every question MUST have exactly 4 choices and exactly one correct answer.\n- Every question MUST have id, question, choices, correctAnswer, explanation.\n- Every chapter MUST have chapterId, title, description, and at least 1 question.\n- Approximately 30 questions per chapter (fewer if the chapter is thin, never fabricate).\n- Balanced A/B/C/D correct-answer positions overall; no obvious answer patterns.\n- All-choice parity: correct answer must not be the longest/most technical/most specific option.\n- Explanations must be grounded in the reference.\n- encyclopedia MUST contain the important terms from the reference, at least 10 entries unless the reference is very small.\n- The JSON MUST be valid. Check it before writing.\n\nAfter writing the file, reply with a one-line confirmation telling me the exact path of the JSON file you wrote.\" 2>&1\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":55,"totalLines":55,"truncated":false}},"title":"xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\opencode.log","time":{"start":1789817810216,"end":1789817810230}},"id":"prt_0b9746c82001faijDLQqYM6yKQ","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b9745fbc0013AdEby4QIaebfF"}}
