{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789818230265,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_7bc5c1318f054b64b64f1dd5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"[\n  {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q16\",\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is one of the four common EA pitfalls described in the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Ivory-tower architecture\",\n        \"Overfunded business cases\",\n        \"Excessive stakeholder reviews\",\n        \"Excessive documentation updates\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"The four pitfalls are ivory-tower architecture, no executive sponsor, big-bang scope, and stale artifacts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q17\",\n      \"question\": \"A business capability map describes what the firm does, such as Marketing -> Lead Generation -> Campaign Management. Which artifact class does it belong to?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A Diagram / Model\",\n        \"A Catalog\",\n        \"A Matrix\",\n        \"A Roadmap\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"The Business Capability Map is a Catalog: a hierarchical decomposition of what the business does to fulfill its mission.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q18\",\n      \"question\": \"Which success factor emphasizes that architecture reviews must be part of approval, not optional?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Small increments\",\n        \"Reviews at project gates\",\n        \"Active sponsor\",\n        \"A living repository\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Reviews at project gates are a success factor: they are part of approval, not optional.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q19\",\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is one of the four main areas of security in the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Data Security\",\n        \"Budget Security\",\n        \"Vendor Security\",\n        \"Sprint Security\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"The four areas are Data Security, Network/Technology Security, Application Security, and Physical Security.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q20\",\n      \"question\": \"HR staff should only access HR data, not finance data. Which concept does this scenario illustrate?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Authentication\",\n        \"Role-based access control (RBAC)\",\n        \"Physical security\",\n        \"Encryption at rest\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"RBAC means people only get access to what they need for their job, as in the HR staff vs finance data example.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q21\",\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is TRUE about security in enterprise architecture?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Security should be considered after implementation to avoid delays\",\n        \"Security tasks should be part of the project timeline, not an afterthought\",\n        \"Security is handled by a separate department with no EA input\",\n        \"Security only matters for physical hardware\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Security should be considered while implementing the architecture, and security tasks should be part of the project timeline, not an afterthought.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q22\",\n      \"question\": \"Which core repository component defines the schema, entity types, taxonomy, and relationship rules for artifacts?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Architecture Landscape\",\n        \"Architecture Metamodel\",\n        \"Governance & Standards\",\n        \"Reference Architecture\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"The Architecture Metamodel defines the underlying schema, entity types, taxonomy, and relationship rules for how artifacts connect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q23\",\n      \"question\": \"Which EA support tool capability generates dynamic visual models directly from repository data?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Impact & Risk Analysis\",\n        \"Automated Diagramming & Layout\",\n        \"Collaborative Governance\",\n        \"Automated Data Ingestion\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Automated Diagramming & Layout generates dynamic visual models directly from repository data, keeping diagrams synchronized.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q24\",\n      \"question\": \"Which support tool is the free, open-source, lightweight option known for ArchiMate modeling?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"LeanIX\",\n        \"Software AG Alfabet\",\n        \"Archi\",\n        \"Sparx Enterprise Architect\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Archi is the free, open-source, lightweight graphical modeling tool for ArchiMate modeling.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q25\",\n      \"question\": \"Which EA support tool is focused on strategic IT governance and portfolio management for large enterprises and financial institutions?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"LeanIX\",\n        \"Sparx Enterprise Architect\",\n        \"Software AG Alfabet\",\n        \"Archi\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Software AG Alfabet focuses on strategic IT governance and portfolio management, with robust financial planning and risk alignment for large/financial firms.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q26\",\n      \"question\": \"Which statement best describes the 'impact & risk analysis' capability of EA support tools?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"It runs traceability queries to evaluate how modifying an application impacts connected systems\",\n        \"It automatically draws network diagrams from cloud data\",\n        \"It connects via APIs to CMDBs to refresh landscape data\",\n        \"It provides role-based access for review boards\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Impact & Risk Analysis performs traceability queries to evaluate how replacing or modifying an application impacts connected systems and operations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q27\",\n      \"question\": \"In the repository governance lifecycle, what does the 'Compliance Check' stage perform?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Connects to cloud platforms to refresh data\",\n        \"Provides approval workflows and audit trails for ARB approvals\",\n        \"Generates dynamic visual models from repository data\",\n        \"Runs traceability queries to evaluate the impact of modifying applications\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n      \"explanation\": \"The Compliance Check stage performs traceability queries to evaluate how replacing or modifying an application impacts connected systems and operations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q28\",\n      \"question\": \"What does integrating the EA repository with Jira, Confluence, and CI/CD pipelines achieve?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Planned architecture guards are pushed into developer workflows\",\n        \"Cloud resources are automatically procured\",\n        \"Repository data is encrypted at rest\",\n        \"Stakeholder meetings are scheduled automatically\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"SDLC & DevOps alignment ensures developer compliance; architectural guardrails are pushed directly into developer workflows.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q29\",\n      \"question\": \"Which scenario best illustrates CMDB & ITSM synchronization?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Reconciling planned architecture with actual runtime reality via ServiceNow or AWS Config\",\n        \"Publishing the future view every six months\",\n        \"Assigning RBAC roles to HR staff\",\n        \"Running a CONOPS storytelling session\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Bi-directional CMDB integration reconciles planned architecture with actual runtime reality, verifying deployed assets match strategic models.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch3-q30\",\n      \"question\": \"According to the reference, what happens to IT spend when projects must trace back to business goals?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"IT spending increases for all departments\",\n        \"Duplicate and siloed systems stop being bought and built\",\n        \"Budgets are tied to vendor offerings\",\n        \"Spending is capped at the infrastructure layer\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Tying every peso of IT spending to a business goal stops duplicate and siloed systems from being bought and built.\"\n    }\n]","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch3b.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch3b.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch3b.json","time":{"start":1789818230249,"end":1789818230263}},"id":"prt_0b97a9daf0017iOBZAnKcquhnM","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b97a97180012c1gB2qk75bydz"}}
