{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789818248811,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_e05b557d1c244e53a37531aa","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"chapterId\": \"ch4\",\n  \"title\": \"L5 — All About Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA)\",\n  \"description\": \"SOA principles, components, communication patterns, REST vs SOAP, the Enterprise Service Bus, and the evolution from monolithic to SOA to microservices.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q01\",\n      \"question\": \"What is a 'service' in the context of SOA?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A computer program that exposes full internal logic\",\n        \"A software component assigned a task that is reusable and modular\",\n        \"A database table shared across all consumers\",\n        \"A one-time integration between two systems\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"A service is a software component assigned a task, used to make components reusable and modular for faster development.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q02\",\n      \"question\": \"Which scenario best illustrates the SOA principle of Reusability?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A payment service is used by both a website and a mobile app\",\n        \"A service hides its internal implementation from consumers\",\n        \"A large system is split into several small services\",\n        \"A service stores state from past transactions\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Reusability means using a service in multiple parts of the system, as with the Website -> Payment Service <- Mobile App example.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q03\",\n      \"question\": \"Which SOA principle requires that a service change should not affect other components using it?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Abstraction\",\n        \"Modularity\",\n        \"Loose Coupling\",\n        \"Reusability\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Loose coupling ensures changes in one service do not affect other components using it; services should also be stateless.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q04\",\n      \"question\": \"Which statement best describes the Abstraction principle in SOA?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Consumers see the full implementation so they can debug\",\n        \"Clients cannot see the important logic or code behind a service\",\n        \"Each service manages its own database\",\n        \"Services communicate through a central bus\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Abstraction means customers and clients should not be able to see important logic or code; the app only needs the interface details.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q05\",\n      \"question\": \"Which SOA component creates, maintains, and provides a service?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Service Consumer\",\n        \"Service Registry\",\n        \"Service Provider\",\n        \"Service Broker\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"The Service Provider creates, maintains, and provides a service, such as a company providing a Payment Service.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q06\",\n      \"question\": \"Which SOA component acts as a directory of available services and how to access them?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Service Consumer\",\n        \"Service Registry\",\n        \"Service Provider\",\n        \"Service Mesh\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"The Service Registry acts as a directory of available services, containing information about what is available and how consumers can access them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q07\",\n      \"question\": \"In which communication mode does the caller send a request and wait for an immediate reply before continuing?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Asynchronous / Message-Based\",\n        \"Synchronous\",\n        \"Event-driven streaming\",\n        \"Batch processing\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Synchronous communication sends a request and waits for an immediate reply before continuing; it is common with REST APIs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q08\",\n      \"question\": \"Which mechanism lets consumers locate providers at runtime instead of a hard-coded address?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Service Discovery\",\n        \"Load Balancing\",\n        \"Protocol Mediation\",\n        \"Fair queuing\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Service Discovery lets consumers locate providers at runtime through a service registry (e.g., UDDI) instead of a hard-coded address.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q09\",\n      \"question\": \"Which statement about REST is TRUE according to the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"It is a strict, formal messaging standard\",\n        \"It always uses XML envelopes\",\n        \"It is an architectural style that uses standard HTTP verbs\",\n        \"It requires WS-Security for every message\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"REST is an architectural style, not a strict standard, and typically uses JSON over standard HTTP verbs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q10\",\n      \"question\": \"Which statement about SOAP is TRUE according to the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"It is lighter than REST and uses JSON\",\n        \"It has built-in standards for security and transactions\",\n        \"It is stateless by design with no security options\",\n        \"It only works over HTTP\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"SOAP is a strict, formal messaging standard with built-in standards for security (WS-Security) and transactions; it works over multiple transports.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q11\",\n      \"question\": \"Which system type would MOST appropriately use SOAP over REST based on the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A mobile game leaderboard\",\n        \"A public news feed website\",\n        \"A banking system requiring high reliability\",\n        \"A simple contact form\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"SOAP best suits enterprise systems needing high reliability such as banking and finance, while REST suits simpler, faster web and mobile APIs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q12\",\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a core function of the Enterprise Service Bus (ESB)?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Transformation of data formats like XML to JSON\",\n        \"Creating new business processes\",\n        \"Storing all service credentials\",\n        \"Replacing the service registry\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"The six ESB functions include routing, transformation, protocol mediation, orchestration, monitoring & logging, and security enforcement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q13\",\n      \"question\": \"Which ESB function coordinates calls to multiple services in sequence to complete a single business process?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Routing\",\n        \"Orchestration\",\n        \"Protocol Mediation\",\n        \"Transformation\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Orchestration coordinates calls to multiple services in sequence to complete a single business process.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q14\",\n      \"question\": \"Which ESB function bridges services that use different transport protocols such as HTTP, JMS, or FTP?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Protocol Mediation\",\n        \"Routing\",\n        \"Monitoring & Logging\",\n        \"Security Enforcement\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Protocol Mediation bridges services that use different transport protocols, such as HTTP, JMS, or FTP.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch4-q15\",\n      \"question\": \"In the ESB architecture diagram, how do the Web App, Mobile App, CRM, and Legacy System communicate with the Payment, Inventory, and Shipping services?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Each app connects directly to the service it needs\",\n        \"All communication flows through the ESB, and no service calls another directly\",\n        \"The legacy system bypasses the bus for speed\",\n        \"The CRM connects only to the Payment service\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"All communication flows through the Enterprise Service Bus; no service calls another directly.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch4a.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch4a.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch4a.json","time":{"start":1789818248791,"end":1789818248808}},"id":"prt_0b97adbb4001lG8ez66IhvPxjI","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b97ad67200100ERWhQYWKW2Ae"}}
