{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789818285381,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_4c3efa24a08647bf916237a0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"[\n  {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q16\",\n      \"question\": \"Invoices, purchase orders, and config files have a regular, predictable structure where order does not matter. How are these XML documents classified?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Document-centric XML\",\n        \"Data-centric XML\",\n        \"Mixed content XML\",\n        \"Native XML\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Data-centric XML has a regular, predictable structure where order doesn't matter, so it suits a relational database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q17\",\n      \"question\": \"Manuals, contracts, and articles have irregular, mixed content where order matters. These are best stored in:\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A native XML database\",\n        \"A relational table\",\n        \"A spreadsheet\",\n        \"A content-addressed store\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Document-centric XML with irregular content and order sensitivity is best stored in a native XML database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q18\",\n      \"question\": \"Which XML storage technique breaks the tree into rows and columns, making the original document no longer exist?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Native tree\",\n        \"CLOB / text column\",\n        \"Shredding\",\n        \"BLOB storage\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Shredding breaks the XML tree into rows and columns, enabling fast joins and reports, but the original document no longer exists.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q19\",\n      \"question\": \"Which storage approach keeps the whole document in one column while also copying key fields into normal columns?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"XML-enabled database\",\n        \"Hybrid / XML column\",\n        \"Native XML database\",\n        \"Shredded tables\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"The hybrid / XML column approach keeps the whole document in one column and copies key fields into normal columns, trading fidelity and speed at the cost of duplication.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q20\",\n      \"question\": \"Which standardized format family does the reference associate with global interbank payments?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"HL7 / CDA\",\n        \"RosettaNet / ebXML\",\n        \"ISO 20022\",\n        \"OpenAPI\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"ISO 20022 is the standardized format for global interbank payments.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q21\",\n      \"question\": \"Which standardized format family is used for healthcare and clinical data?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"HL7 / CDA\",\n        \"ISO 20022\",\n        \"RosettaNet / ebXML\",\n        \"SMTP\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"HL7 / CDA is the standardized format family for healthcare and clinical data.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q22\",\n      \"question\": \"What was UDDI created for?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"To encrypt SOAP messages in transit\",\n        \"To help organizations publish and discover web services\",\n        \"To define the XML vocabulary for banking\",\n        \"To convert XML into HTML\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"UDDI (Universal Description, Discovery, and Integration) was a directory where businesses could publish and discover web services.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q23\",\n      \"question\": \"What does WSDL provide for a SOAP web service?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Encryption keys for secure messaging\",\n        \"A technical contract describing services, operations, and access\",\n        \"A runtime registry of available instances\",\n        \"An HTTP transport layer\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"WSDL acts like a technical contract describing what services are available, what operations they support, and how they can be accessed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q24\",\n      \"question\": \"Which WS-* specification adds authentication, encryption, and message integrity to SOAP messages?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"WS-ReliableMessaging\",\n        \"WSDL\",\n        \"WS-Security\",\n        \"UDDI\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"WS-Security adds authentication, encryption, and message integrity to SOAP messages, often paired with SAML assertions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q25\",\n      \"question\": \"Which WS-* specification ensures messages are still delivered correctly even over unstable networks?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"WS-Security\",\n        \"WS-ReliableMessaging\",\n        \"WSDL\",\n        \"WS-Policy\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"WS-ReliableMessaging ensures messages are delivered correctly even over unstable networks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q26\",\n      \"question\": \"In web services integration, which approach uses a central process that directs how services interact from the top down?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Choreography\",\n        \"P2P federation\",\n        \"Orchestration\",\n        \"Data binding\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Orchestration relies on a central process that directs how different services interact, coordinating them from the top down.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q27\",\n      \"question\": \"Which integration approach lets services communicate directly with one another in a peer-to-peer manner with no single controlling process?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Orchestration\",\n        \"Choreography\",\n        \"Orchestration bus\",\n        \"Hub-and-spoke\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Choreography lets services communicate directly peer-to-peer with no single controlling process.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q28\",\n      \"question\": \"Why does the reference describe XML as the 'lingua franca' of enterprise integration?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"It is the fastest binary format\",\n        \"It is the official standard of one vendor\",\n        \"It requires a specific operating system\",\n        \"It is a vendor-neutral, self-describing common language any platform can interpret\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 3,\n      \"explanation\": \"XML acts as a vendor-neutral, self-describing common language with explicit tags that any hardware or software platform can interpret.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q29\",\n      \"question\": \"How does XSLT help bridge differing enterprise schemas without modifying original databases?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"It renames database tables for the new schema\",\n        \"It converts supplier PO formats to canonical enterprise standards\",\n        \"It drops incompatible rows from the database\",\n        \"It locks the database while the schema changes\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"XSLT transforms supplier PO formats to canonical enterprise standards, mapping incompatible field names automatically.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch5-q30\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the primary difference between a well-formed and a valid XML document?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Valid requires every attribute to be repeated\",\n        \"Well-formed requires a schema\",\n        \"Valid means well-formed AND follows a schema\",\n        \"Well-formed invalidates namespaces\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Well-formed documents meet syntax rules; valid documents are well-formed AND follow a schema (only allowed elements present, values matching types).\"\n    }\n]","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch5b.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch5b.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch5b.json","time":{"start":1789818285371,"end":1789818285379}},"id":"prt_0b97b815a001cfYW3c5cEmjyt5","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b97b7afc001Nb5Uhd7pCDCrFV"}}
