{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789818325004,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_8fe620c5bb6e49ef80b7eeb8","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"chapterId\": \"ch7\",\n  \"title\": \"L8 — Enterprise Integration\",\n  \"description\": \"Enterprise integration fundamentals, XML integration best practices, web services and APIs, SOAP vs REST, security and authentication, and the Service-Oriented Enterprise.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q01\",\n      \"question\": \"What is the key idea behind Enterprise Integration according to the reference?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Replacing existing systems with one platform\",\n        \"Connecting, not replacing, existing systems\",\n        \"Deleting legacy systems entirely\",\n        \"Standardizing every system's data format\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"The key idea is that integration is about connecting, not replacing, existing systems.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q02\",\n      \"question\": \"Why do companies need integration even though each system works on its own?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Because systems already share consistent records\",\n        \"Because data silos cause duplicate entries and inconsistent records\",\n        \"Because every system uses a common database\",\n        \"Because manual copying is always accurate\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Many systems don't talk to each other, producing data silos, duplicate entries, and inconsistent records that integration removes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q03\",\n      \"question\": \"Which of the following is a benefit of enterprise integration?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"More manual work and errors\",\n        \"Slower decision-making\",\n        \"Real-time data sharing\",\n        \"Reduced customer service\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"Benefits include real-time data sharing, faster decisions, reduced manual work/errors, cost savings, and better customer service.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q04\",\n      \"question\": \"Which failure mode results from one field using different tags across systems?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Mapping breaks silently\",\n        \"Payloads compress faster\",\n        \"Schemas always validate\",\n        \"Monitoring improves automatically\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Inconsistent data — the same field with different tags across systems — causes mapping to break silently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q05\",\n      \"question\": \"Which practice helps maintain clear structure in XML?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Using short cryptic tags to reduce file size\",\n        \"Using meaningful names like <shippingAddress> and a logical hierarchy\",\n        \"Duplicating values for every recipient\",\n        \"Nesting every element five levels deep\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Clear structure uses meaningful names (e.g., <shippingAddress>, not <sa>) and a logical hierarchy with flat, DRY content.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q06\",\n      \"question\": \"Which layered validation is recommended before accepting an XML payload?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Well-formed syntax, schema (XSD) check, required fields and types\",\n        \"File size and read speed only\",\n        \"Compression ratio and encoding only\",\n        \"Storage cost and backup count\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Recommended validation is layered: well-formed syntax, schema (XSD) check, matching tags and root, and required fields and types.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q07\",\n      \"question\": \"Which security measure protects XML data in transit?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Using HTTPS\",\n        \"Increasing file nesting\",\n        \"Removing all tags\",\n        \"Disabling authentication\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"SSL/TLS (HTTPS) encrypts the XML in transit; the reference says to protect every hop.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q08\",\n      \"question\": \"Why should seemingly harmless external entities in XML be disabled?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"To reduce the number of tags\",\n        \"To block XML injection attacks\",\n        \"To speed up gzip compression\",\n        \"To make messages more readable\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Blocking XML attacks includes disabling external entities and capping size/depth to prevent injection and disclosure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q09\",\n      \"question\": \"For large XML collections, which performance approach is recommended?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Always load the full DOM\",\n        \"Paginate or stream large collections, and gzip when useful\",\n        \"Send the entire file uncompressed\",\n        \"Embed all data into one attribute\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Performance guidance: send only necessary data, keep XML reasonably sized, paginate/stream large collections, and gzip when useful.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q10\",\n      \"question\": \"What should an error response provide for good XML error handling?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A generic error code\",\n        \"A specific, actionable message\",\n        \"The full stack trace\",\n        \"No message at all\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Error handling should give clear, specific, actionable feedback rather than a generic error code.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q11\",\n      \"question\": \"Which comparison correctly describes authentication vs authorization?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Authentication asks 'what can you do?'; authorization asks 'who are you?'\",\n        \"Authentication asks 'who are you?'; authorization asks 'what can you do?'\",\n        \"Both ask who the user is\",\n        \"Both ask what the user can do\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Authentication = 'who are you?'; Authorization = 'what can you do?'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q12\",\n      \"question\": \"Which statement about REST and SOAP is TRUE in the L8 comparison?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"REST supports only XML\",\n        \"SOAP is an architectural style\",\n        \"SOAP is slower because of heavier messages\",\n        \"REST must always use XML and JSON together\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 2,\n      \"explanation\": \"SOAP is a protocol with built-in security and heavier XML messages, making it slower; REST is a lighter architectural style.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q13\",\n      \"question\": \"Which example best fits where SOAP should be used over REST?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"A social media feed\",\n        \"An interbank transfer system\",\n        \"A mobile game leaderboard\",\n        \"A weather widget\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"SOAP fits banking, enterprise, and government use, such as interbank transfer systems; REST suits web and mobile apps.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q14\",\n      \"question\": \"Which mechanism is commonly used for authentication in modern APIs?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"OAuth 2.0 and JWT\",\n        \"gzip compression\",\n        \"CDN caching\",\n        \"Load balancing\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Authentication approaches include API keys, OAuth 2.0, JWT, and Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ch7-q15\",\n      \"question\": \"Which practice helps prevent SQL injection and XSS?\",\n      \"choices\": [\n        \"Rate limiting\",\n        \"Input validation\",\n        \"Pagination\",\n        \"GZIP compression\"\n      ],\n      \"correctAnswer\": 1,\n      \"explanation\": \"Input validation prevents SQL Injection and XSS; rate limiting and firewalls prevent abuse and DDoS.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","filePath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch7a.json"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch7a.json","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch7a.json","time":{"start":1789818324993,"end":1789818325001}},"id":"prt_0b97c1ddd001NF1ZoHYTB2qdu5","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b97c193a001Inrp8QcyJWBGTs"}}
