{"type":"text","timestamp":1789818445374,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"id":"prt_0b97deccb0017xHAx87QJOwG4r","messageID":"msg_0b97d387f001rWKH0WnZROl5Yt","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Generate a complete interactive comprehensive exam question bank (~30 questions × 7 chapters + encyclopedia) for the \"SAI 1 — System Architecture and Integration 1 (ITNET312-T)\" reviewer, then write it as one valid `questions.json` to `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\questions.json` following the `interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator` skill and the `worker.php` prompt schema.\n\n## Important Details\n- The model cannot read PDF input directly; the 43-page PDF was extracted to text via Python (pymupdf/fitz) into `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\source.txt` (131,065 chars) and fully read. Delete this artifact when done.\n- The PDF is the PRIMARY SOURCE OF TRUTH (do not invent facts). It covers 7 lessons → 7 chapters: ch1=L2 Enterprise Architecture Components, ch2=L3 Developing an EA, ch3=L4 Using an EA, ch4=L5 All About SOA, ch5=L6 Integrating Technology (XML/web services), ch6=L7 Integrating Applications, ch7=L8 Enterprise Integration.\n- Required final schema: `{title, subject, summary, chapters:[{chapterId, title, description, questions:[{id, question, choices[], correctAnswer (0-based int), explanation}]}], encyclopedia:[{chapterId, term, definition}]}`.\n- Skill rules: ~30 questions/chapter, exactly 4 choices with exactly one correct, no keyword leakage/parity bias (equal length & technicality), balanced A/B/C/D positions per chapter (~8/8/7/7), explanations for every question, stable IDs (`chN-qNN`), encyclopedia ≥10 entries.\n- The Write tool truncates very large single writes (first attempt failed: \"JSON Parse error: Unterminated string\"). Therefore fragments are written as ~15 questions per file: `chNa.json` = full chapter object (Q1–15), `chNb.json` = plain JSON array (Q16–30).\n- ch1 answer-position audit is imbalanced (A=3, B=9, C=11, D=7); plan is to rebalance programmatically during merge by rotating each question's choices (safe because exam-app.js shuffles choices AND question order at runtime).\n- The worker (opencode.exe run) only expects `questions.json` written; do NOT create other files in the exam dir and do NOT print the JSON in the final reply.\n- Environment: Python 3.11.9; pypdf/PyPDF2/pymupdf/pdfplumber available; `pdftotext` NOT available. Job `test001` status currently `running` in status.json.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- Loaded skill; explored project (worker.php, index.php, exam.php, api/data.php, lib/config.php, lib/db.php, assets/exam-app.js); read job.json (id=test001, title \"SAI Reviewer Test\").\n- Extracted and read full PDF text; planned 7 chapters and coverage per chapter.\n- Created build dir `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build`.\n- Written fragments: ch1a.json & ch1b.json (ch1 Q1–30), ch2a.json & ch2b.json (ch2 Q1–30), ch3a.json & ch3b.json (ch3 Q1–30), ch4a.json & ch4b.json (ch4 Q1–30), ch5a.json & ch5b.json (ch5 Q1–30), ch6a.json (ch6 Q1–15).\n- Determined merge plan: combine fragments via Python, validate schema, rebalance answer positions, anti-guessing audit, write final questions.json, clean up.\n\n### Active\n- Authoring ch6b.json (ch6 Q16–30) — not yet written.\n- ch7 (L8) fragments not yet written.\n- Encyclopedia fragments not yet authored.\n- Merge/validation/rebalance script not yet run; final questions.json not yet written.\n\n### Blocked\n- No blockers; remaining work is large authoring volume (ch6b, ch7a, ch7b, encyclopedia) plus merge/validation/cleanup.\n\n## Next Move\n1. Write `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\ch6b.json` — array of ch6 Q16–30 (EAI objectives, integration architectures ESB/Hub-and-Spoke/SOA/EDA, EIP patterns: messaging channels, content-based router, message translator, publish-subscribe; benefits/challenges/best practices; integration strategies; choosing a strategy).\n2. Write `ch7a.json` (object, Q1–15) and `ch7b.json` (array, Q16–30) for ch7=L8 Enterprise Integration (XML integration best practices & failure modes, clear structure, validation & security incl. XML attacks, performance & error handling, web services/APIs REST/SOAP/GraphQL, auth vs authorization, reliability & performance, SOE components and 6 build steps, benefits/challenges).\n3. Author encyclopedia fragments (per-chapter terms, definitions grounded in reference).\n4. Write and run a Python merge+validate script: build final JSON, validate schema (4 choices, int correctAnswer 0–3, non-empty fields), rebalance answer letters per chapter to ~8/8/7/7 by rotating choices, run anti-guessing audit (option length/keyword parallelism).\n5. Write final bank to `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\questions.json` and verify JSON validity.\n6. Clean up `sai_build` temp dir and `source.txt`; update todo list.\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\job.json` — job config; points to output file.\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\source.pdf` — reference material (primary source of truth).\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\source.txt` — extracted text artifact (delete at end).\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\questions.json` — final deliverable (not yet written).\n- `C:\\Users\\kelly\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\opencode\\sai_build\\` — fragment JSON files (ch1a–ch6a exist; ch6b/ch7a/ch7b pending).\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\.opencode\\skills\\interactive-comprehensive-exam-generator\\SKILL.md` — skill rules (70,571 bytes; read only partially).\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\worker.php` — pipeline that invokes opencode and defines the expected JSON schema/output path.\n- `C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\assets\\exam-app.js` — front-end renderer expecting the final schema; shuffles question and choice order at runtime.","time":{"start":1789818432715,"end":1789818445334}}}
