{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789818483863,"sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_f32c49ebb6724a069d8310ab","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"python -c \"\nimport json\nd = json.load(open(r'C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\questions.json', encoding='utf-8'))\ntargets = {'ch1-q20','ch1-q21','ch1-q29','ch2-q08','ch2-q23','ch3-q01','ch3-q09','ch3-q11','ch3-q18','ch3-q20','ch4-q11','ch5-q05','ch5-q19','ch5-q29','ch6-q15','ch6-q29','ch7-q09','ch7-q16'}\nfor c in d['chapters']:\n    for q in c['questions']:\n        if q['id'] in targets:\n            print(q['id'], '| correct=', chr(65+q['correctAnswer']))\n            print('  Q:', q['question'])\n            for i, chc in enumerate(q['choices']):\n                print(f'   {chr(65+i)}: ({len(chc)}) {chc}')\n            print()\n\""},"output":"ch1-q20 | correct= B\r\n  Q: In the Zachman Framework, which row represents the perspective of the 'Enterprise (Actual System)'?\r\n   A: (8) Designer\r\n   B: (10) Enterprise\r\n   C: (7) Builder\r\n   D: (14) Sub-Contractor\r\n\r\nch1-q21 | correct= C\r\n  Q: Which statement best describes the role of Requirements Management within the TOGAF ADM cycle?\r\n   A: (42) It is applied only once after Phase H ends\r\n   B: (52) It operates only during Phase A, Architecture Vision\r\n   C: (70) It operates throughout all ADM phases and tracks changing requirements\r\n   D: (42) It replaces the Preliminary Phase entirely\r\n\r\nch1-q29 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which artifact category is an Application-to-Function Matrix an example of?\r\n   A: (8) A Matrix\r\n   B: (9) A Diagram\r\n   C: (7) A Model\r\n   D: (9) A Catalog\r\n\r\nch2-q08 | correct= C\r\n  Q: Why are future enterprise architectural views important?\r\n   A: (35) They replace the EA Management Plan\r\n   B: (47) They document exactly what already exists today\r\n   C: (82) They support resource planning, decision-making, and enterprise-wide communication\r\n   D: (55) They eliminate the need for current-state documentation\r\n\r\nch2-q23 | correct= B\r\n  Q: What should be documented in a separate IT Security Plan instead of the main architecture summary?\r\n   A: (16) Workforce skills\r\n   B: (26) Sensitive security details\r\n   C: (21) Business capabilities\r\n   D: (20) Technology standards\r\n\r\nch3-q01 | correct= D\r\n  Q: Which statement best describes what Enterprise Architecture provides to an organization?\r\n   A: (41) A replacement for all legacy applications\r\n   B: (40) A mandatory federal compliance framework\r\n   C: (34) A pricing model for cloud services\r\n   D: (63) A blueprint showing how parts of the organization work together\r\n\r\nch3-q09 | correct= A\r\n  Q: An enterprise must enforce a compliance deadline from the Data Privacy Act. Based on sequencing tests, how should this work be treated?\r\n   A: (45) As non-negotiable work that must be scheduled\r\n   B: (35) As a dependency for every dashboard\r\n   C: (26) As an optional enhancement\r\n   D: (32) As a pilot first, then a rollout\r\n\r\nch3-q11 | correct= C\r\n  Q: In the 'From Architecture to Projects' process, what does Gap Analysis do?\r\n   A: (48) Attaches cost, benefit, and risk to each package\r\n   B: (59) Places packages on a timeline with transition architectures\r\n   C: (78) Compares As-Is against To-Be to find what is missing, duplicated, and obsolete\r\n   D: (42) Assigns a single owner to each deliverable\r\n\r\nch3-q18 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Which success factor emphasizes that architecture reviews must be part of approval, not optional?\r\n   A: (16) Small increments\r\n   B: (24) Reviews at project gates\r\n   C: (14) Active sponsor\r\n   D: (19) A living repository\r\n\r\nch3-q20 | correct= C\r\n  Q: HR staff should only access HR data, not finance data. Which concept does this scenario illustrate?\r\n   A: (18) Encryption at rest\r\n   B: (14) Authentication\r\n   C: (32) Role-based access control (RBAC)\r\n   D: (17) Physical security\r\n\r\nch4-q11 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which system type would MOST appropriately use SOAP over REST based on the reference?\r\n   A: (43) A banking system requiring high reliability\r\n   B: (21) A simple contact form\r\n   C: (25) A mobile game leaderboard\r\n   D: (26) A public news feed website\r\n\r\nch5-q05 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Having exactly one outermost element with everything else inside it is a requirement for:\r\n   A: (13) The attribute\r\n   B: (16) The root element\r\n   C: (10) The prolog\r\n   D: (13) The namespace\r\n\r\nch5-q19 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Which storage approach keeps the whole document in one column while also copying key fields into normal columns?\r\n   A: (20) XML-enabled database\r\n   B: (19) Hybrid / XML column\r\n   C: (19) Native XML database\r\n   D: (15) Shredded tables\r\n\r\nch5-q29 | correct= C\r\n  Q: How does XSLT help bridge differing enterprise schemas without modifying original databases?\r\n   A: (46) It locks the database while the schema changes\r\n   B: (45) It renames database tables for the new schema\r\n   C: (65) It converts supplier PO formats to canonical enterprise standards\r\n   D: (44) It drops incompatible rows from the database\r\n\r\nch6-q15 | correct= D\r\n  Q: Which incremental modernization pattern minimizes operational risk when migrating legacy systems?\r\n   A: (19) Full mirror cutover\r\n   B: (19) Parallel code forks\r\n   C: (20) Big-bang replacement\r\n   D: (21) Strangler Fig pattern\r\n\r\nch6-q29 | correct= A\r\n  Q: What does iPaaS (Integration Platform as a Service) provide?\r\n   A: (97) A cloud-hosted toolset connecting applications and data across cloud and on-premises environments\r\n   B: (38) A local firewall for internal networks\r\n   C: (38) A relational database with XML columns\r\n   D: (30) A manual file transfer service\r\n\r\nch7-q09 | correct= B\r\n  Q: For large XML collections, which performance approach is recommended?\r\n   A: (24) Always load the full DOM\r\n   B: (58) Paginate or stream large collections, and gzip when useful\r\n   C: (33) Send the entire file uncompressed\r\n   D: (33) Embed all data into one attribute\r\n\r\nch7-q16 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which reliability mechanism does the reference associate with message queuing tools like RabbitMQ and Kafka?\r\n   A: (15) Message queuing\r\n   B: (15) GZIP pagination\r\n   C: (20) CDN content delivery\r\n   D: (31) Redundancy and failover systems\r\n\r\n","metadata":{"output":"ch1-q20 | correct= B\r\n  Q: In the Zachman Framework, which row represents the perspective of the 'Enterprise (Actual System)'?\r\n   A: (8) Designer\r\n   B: (10) Enterprise\r\n   C: (7) Builder\r\n   D: (14) Sub-Contractor\r\n\r\nch1-q21 | correct= C\r\n  Q: Which statement best describes the role of Requirements Management within the TOGAF ADM cycle?\r\n   A: (42) It is applied only once after Phase H ends\r\n   B: (52) It operates only during Phase A, Architecture Vision\r\n   C: (70) It operates throughout all ADM phases and tracks changing requirements\r\n   D: (42) It replaces the Preliminary Phase entirely\r\n\r\nch1-q29 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which artifact category is an Application-to-Function Matrix an example of?\r\n   A: (8) A Matrix\r\n   B: (9) A Diagram\r\n   C: (7) A Model\r\n   D: (9) A Catalog\r\n\r\nch2-q08 | correct= C\r\n  Q: Why are future enterprise architectural views important?\r\n   A: (35) They replace the EA Management Plan\r\n   B: (47) They document exactly what already exists today\r\n   C: (82) They support resource planning, decision-making, and enterprise-wide communication\r\n   D: (55) They eliminate the need for current-state documentation\r\n\r\nch2-q23 | correct= B\r\n  Q: What should be documented in a separate IT Security Plan instead of the main architecture summary?\r\n   A: (16) Workforce skills\r\n   B: (26) Sensitive security details\r\n   C: (21) Business capabilities\r\n   D: (20) Technology standards\r\n\r\nch3-q01 | correct= D\r\n  Q: Which statement best describes what Enterprise Architecture provides to an organization?\r\n   A: (41) A replacement for all legacy applications\r\n   B: (40) A mandatory federal compliance framework\r\n   C: (34) A pricing model for cloud services\r\n   D: (63) A blueprint showing how parts of the organization work together\r\n\r\nch3-q09 | correct= A\r\n  Q: An enterprise must enforce a compliance deadline from the Data Privacy Act. Based on sequencing tests, how should this work be treated?\r\n   A: (45) As non-negotiable work that must be scheduled\r\n   B: (35) As a dependency for every dashboard\r\n   C: (26) As an optional enhancement\r\n   D: (32) As a pilot first, then a rollout\r\n\r\nch3-q11 | correct= C\r\n  Q: In the 'From Architecture to Projects' process, what does Gap Analysis do?\r\n   A: (48) Attaches cost, benefit, and risk to each package\r\n   B: (59) Places packages on a timeline with transition architectures\r\n   C: (78) Compares As-Is against To-Be to find what is missing, duplicated, and obsolete\r\n   D: (42) Assigns a single owner to each deliverable\r\n\r\nch3-q18 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Which success factor emphasizes that architecture reviews must be part of approval, not optional?\r\n   A: (16) Small increments\r\n   B: (24) Reviews at project gates\r\n   C: (14) Active sponsor\r\n   D: (19) A living repository\r\n\r\nch3-q20 | correct= C\r\n  Q: HR staff should only access HR data, not finance data. Which concept does this scenario illustrate?\r\n   A: (18) Encryption at rest\r\n   B: (14) Authentication\r\n   C: (32) Role-based access control (RBAC)\r\n   D: (17) Physical security\r\n\r\nch4-q11 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which system type would MOST appropriately use SOAP over REST based on the reference?\r\n   A: (43) A banking system requiring high reliability\r\n   B: (21) A simple contact form\r\n   C: (25) A mobile game leaderboard\r\n   D: (26) A public news feed website\r\n\r\nch5-q05 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Having exactly one outermost element with everything else inside it is a requirement for:\r\n   A: (13) The attribute\r\n   B: (16) The root element\r\n   C: (10) The prolog\r\n   D: (13) The namespace\r\n\r\nch5-q19 | correct= B\r\n  Q: Which storage approach keeps the whole document in one column while also copying key fields into normal columns?\r\n   A: (20) XML-enabled database\r\n   B: (19) Hybrid / XML column\r\n   C: (19) Native XML database\r\n   D: (15) Shredded tables\r\n\r\nch5-q29 | correct= C\r\n  Q: How does XSLT help bridge differing enterprise schemas without modifying original databases?\r\n   A: (46) It locks the database while the schema changes\r\n   B: (45) It renames database tables for the new schema\r\n   C: (65) It converts supplier PO formats to canonical enterprise standards\r\n   D: (44) It drops incompatible rows from the database\r\n\r\nch6-q15 | correct= D\r\n  Q: Which incremental modernization pattern minimizes operational risk when migrating legacy systems?\r\n   A: (19) Full mirror cutover\r\n   B: (19) Parallel code forks\r\n   C: (20) Big-bang replacement\r\n   D: (21) Strangler Fig pattern\r\n\r\nch6-q29 | correct= A\r\n  Q: What does iPaaS (Integration Platform as a Service) provide?\r\n   A: (97) A cloud-hosted toolset connecting applications and data across cloud and on-premises environments\r\n   B: (38) A local firewall for internal networks\r\n   C: (38) A relational database with XML columns\r\n   D: (30) A manual file transfer service\r\n\r\nch7-q09 | correct= B\r\n  Q: For large XML collections, which performance approach is recommended?\r\n   A: (24) Always load the full DOM\r\n   B: (58) Paginate or stream large collections, and gzip when useful\r\n   C: (33) Send the entire file uncompressed\r\n   D: (33) Embed all data into one attribute\r\n\r\nch7-q16 | correct= A\r\n  Q: Which reliability mechanism does the reference associate with message queuing tools like RabbitMQ and Kafka?\r\n   A: (15) Message queuing\r\n   B: (15) GZIP pagination\r\n   C: (20) CDN content delivery\r\n   D: (31) Redundancy and failover systems\r\n\r\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"python -c \"\nimport json\nd = json.load(open(r'C:\\xampp\\htdocs\\automation\\side-project\\data\\exams\\test001\\questions.json', encoding='utf-8'))\ntargets = {'ch1-q20','ch1-q21','ch1-q29','ch2-q08','ch2-q23','ch3-q01','ch3-q09','ch3-q11','ch3-q18','ch3-q20','ch4-q11','ch5-q05','ch5-q19','ch5-q29','ch6-q15','ch6-q29','ch7-q09','ch7-q16'}\nfor c in d['chapters']:\n    for q in c['questions']:\n        if q['id'] in targets:\n            print(q['id'], '| correct=', chr(65+q['correctAnswer']))\n            print('  Q:', q['question'])\n            for i, chc in enumerate(q['choices']):\n                print(f'   {chr(65+i)}: ({len(chc)}) {chc}')\n            print()\n\"","time":{"start":1789818483360,"end":1789818483831}},"id":"prt_0b97eabac001dE2Fo4l7ulo46s","sessionID":"ses_f468c1d68ffe9hPjm84tFHrrnQ","messageID":"msg_0b97e8824001IzkeAmRSqPpD3u"}}
